diff --git a/cluster/runtime-contract.md b/cluster/runtime-contract.md
index 6d472feeb1e103eb8d7f78962fb5386197ce6733..94052cf64ce6ca977651d368b28aafe477f447b0 100644
--- a/cluster/runtime-contract.md
+++ b/cluster/runtime-contract.md
@@ -225,6 +225,20 @@ the candidate. Every old result root, artifact, configuration and preparation
 receipt remains until an owned reset. These retained receipts are evidence, not
 an application-data downgrade guarantee.
 
+The dedicated KB SSH profile advertises one Ed25519 host key per machine.
+Services and optional DNS guests retain it at `/etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key`
+on their writable root. Nodes retain it at
+`/tank/.vpsfree-kb-ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key` on the existing tank. Node startup
+waits for pool preparation and verifies the mounted storage and private paths
+before generating a missing key. Unavailable or unsafe storage refuses startup;
+it does not generate a key on the volatile root or replace an existing key.
+
+This key policy applies to newly prepared artifacts and later updates that
+preserve its algorithm and paths. Older artifacts with volatile or multiple
+host keys require a fresh instance; the engine does not migrate their keys or
+rewrite retained trust. Rolling back to those configurations does not promise
+SSH continuity.
+
 Each runner attempt is recorded before spawn. Recovery must prove an earlier
 attempt gone before starting another. It never automatically boots the previous
 artifact, replaces a root image or activates a guest profile as a fallback.
